ha256" "5292b9c37a5f7aeb99349d58f34defbe238b8d16bcf2408d3f4f1dbab24a4650"} {"question" "q-7990" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What are the parametric equations of the hyperbola $2{x}^{2}-49{y}^{2}=98?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053984/state.json" "file_sha256" "5292b9c37a5f7aeb99349d58f34defbe238b8d16bcf2408d3f4f1dbab24a4650"} {"question" "q-7990" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The parametric equations of a horizontal hyperbola with Cartesian equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1\n$$\n\nare given by\n\n$$\nx=a\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,y=b\\operatorname{tan}⁡t.\n$$\n\nFirst, we rewrite the equation of our hyperbola in standard form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{x}^{2}-49{y}^{2} & =98 \\\\ \\frac{2{x}^{2}}{98}-\\frac{49{y}^{2}}{98} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{49}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, in our case, we $a=\\sqrt{49}=7$ and $b=\\sqrt{2}.$ Therefore, the parametric equations are\n\n$$\nx=7\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,y=\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{tan}⁡t.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053984/state.json" "file_sha256" "5292b9c37a5f7aeb99349d58f34defbe238b8d16bcf2408d3f4f1dbab24a4650"} {"question" "q-7990" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053984/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c35c5c96549a22aec3fa395d4dac4dd4019a49651a81abae6a45792d1ad3398a"} {"question" "q-7990" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053984/state.json" "file_sha256" "5292b9c37a5f7aeb99349d58f34defbe238b8d16bcf2408d3f4f1dbab24a4650"} {"question" "q-7990" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "x=14\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,y=2\\operatorname{tan}⁡t"] ["math" "x=14\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,y=\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{tan}⁡t"] ["math" "x=7\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,y=2\\operatorname{tan}⁡t"] ["math" "x=7\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,y=\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{tan}⁡t"] ["math" "x=\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,y=7\\operatorname{tan}⁡t"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053984/state.json" "file_sha256" "5292b9c37a5f7aeb99349d58f34defbe238b8d16bcf2408d3f4f1dbab24a4650"} {"question" "q-7990" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "x=7\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,y=\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{tan}⁡t"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053984/state.json" "file_sha256" "5292b9c37a5f7aeb99349d58f34defbe238b8d16bcf2408d3f4f1dbab24a4650"} {"question" "q-274724" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053984/assets/060fcf34b388e42aa557ac8182c724236cf8ec161e37fa4fe1e96a0b63fab44f.png)\n\nComplete the following parametric equations generating the hyperbola above in terms of the parameter $t,$ defined for $t\\in [-\\pi ,\\pi ]$ where $t\\ne \\pm \\frac{\\pi }{2},$ given that its asymptotes are $y=\\pm \\frac{5}{2}x.$\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}\n$\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,y=$\n{{field-2}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053984/state.json" "file_sha256" "5292b9c37a5f7aeb99349d58f34defbe238b8d16bcf2408d3f4f1dbab24a4650"} {"question" "q-274724" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The parametric equations of a horizontal hyperbola centered at the origin with Cartesian equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1\n$$\n\nare given by\n\n$$\nx=a\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,y=b\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ and $b$ are positive constants.\n\nThe vertices of the hyperbola occur at $(\\pm a,0).$ From the graph, we have that $(2,0)$ is a vertex of the hyperbola, so $a=2.$\n\nThe asymptotes of a horizontal hyperbola are $y=\\pm \\frac{b}{a}x.$ In our case, the asymptotes are $y=\\pm \\frac{5}{2}x,$ and so we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{b}{a} & =\\frac{5}{2} \\\\ \\frac{b}{2} & =\\frac{5}{2} \\\\ b & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the parametric equations of the hyperbola are\n\n$$\nx=2\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,y=5\\operatorname{tan}⁡t.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053984/state.json" "file_sha256" "5292b9c37a5f7aeb99349d58f34defbe238b8d16bcf2408d3f4f1dbab24a4650"} {"question" "q-274724" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053984/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c35c5c96549a22aec3fa395d4dac4dd4019a49651a81abae6a45792d1ad3398a"} {"question" "q-274724" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053984/state.json" "file_sha256" "5292b9c37a5f7aeb99349d58f34defbe238b8d16bcf2408d3f4f1dbab24a4650"} {"question" "q-274724" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053984/state.json" "file_sha256" "5292b9c37a5f7aeb99349d58f34defbe238b8d16bcf2408d3f4f1dbab24a4650"} {"question" "q-274724" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "