 parametric equations of the hyperbola are\n\n$$\nx=1\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,y=3\\operatorname{tan}⁡t.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053984/state.json" "file_sha256" "5292b9c37a5f7aeb99349d58f34defbe238b8d16bcf2408d3f4f1dbab24a4650"} {"question" "q-325916" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053984/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c35c5c96549a22aec3fa395d4dac4dd4019a49651a81abae6a45792d1ad3398a"} {"question" "q-325916" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053984/state.json" "file_sha256" "5292b9c37a5f7aeb99349d58f34defbe238b8d16bcf2408d3f4f1dbab24a4650"} {"question" "q-325916" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053984/state.json" "file_sha256" "5292b9c37a5f7aeb99349d58f34defbe238b8d16bcf2408d3f4f1dbab24a4650"} {"question" "q-325916" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053984/state.json" "file_sha256" "5292b9c37a5f7aeb99349d58f34defbe238b8d16bcf2408d3f4f1dbab24a4650"} {"question" "q-325916" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3\\tan(t)"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053984/state.json" "file_sha256" "5292b9c37a5f7aeb99349d58f34defbe238b8d16bcf2408d3f4f1dbab24a4650"} {"question" "q-325926" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053984/assets/bf1ba7913469cf12969f8c0fa546f46b881bd38794c1b7b3d2f7500859d6ad56.png)\n\nComplete the following parametric equations generating the hyperbola above in terms of the parameter $t,$ defined for $t\\in [-\\pi ,\\pi ]$ where $t\\ne \\pm \\frac{\\pi }{2},$ given that its asymptotes are $y=\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{7}}{3}x.$\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}\n$\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,y=$\n{{field-2}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053984/state.json" "file_sha256" "5292b9c37a5f7aeb99349d58f34defbe238b8d16bcf2408d3f4f1dbab24a4650"} {"question" "q-325926" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The parametric equations of a horizontal hyperbola centered at the origin with Cartesian equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1\n$$\n\nare given by\n\n$$\nx=a\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,y=b\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ and $b$ are positive constants.\n\nThe vertices of the hyperbola occur at $(\\pm a,0).$ From the graph, we have that $(3,0)$ is a vertex of the hyperbola, so $a=3.$\n\nThe asymptotes of a horizontal hyperbola are $y=\\pm \\frac{b}{a}x.$ In our case, the asymptotes are $y=\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{7}}{3}x,$ and so we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{b}{a} & =\\frac{\\sqrt{7}}{3} \\\\ \\frac{b}{3} & =\\frac{\\sqrt{7}}{3} \\\\ b & =\\sqrt{7}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the parametric equations of the hyperbola are\n\n$$\nx=3\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,y=\\sqrt{7}\\operatorname{tan}⁡t.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053984/state.json" "file_sha256" "5292b9c37a5f7aeb99349d58f34defbe238b8d16bcf2408d3f4f1dbab24a4650"} {"question" "q-325926" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Cour