}{{b}^{2}}=1\n$$\n\nare given by\n\n$$\nx=a\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,y=b\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ and $b$ are positive constants.\n\nThe vertices of the hyperbola occur at $(\\pm a,0).$ From the graph, we have that $(\\sqrt{6},0)$ is a vertex of the hyperbola, so $a=\\sqrt{6}.$\n\nThe asymptotes of a horizontal hyperbola are $y=\\pm \\frac{b}{a}x.$ In our case, the asymptotes are $y=\\pm \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{6}}x,$ and so we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{b}{a} & =\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{6}} \\\\ \\frac{b}{\\sqrt{6}} & =\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{6}} \\\\ b & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the parametric equations of the hyperbola are\n\n$$\nx=\\sqrt{6}\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,y=2\\operatorname{tan}⁡t.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053984/state.json" "file_sha256" "5292b9c37a5f7aeb99349d58f34defbe238b8d16bcf2408d3f4f1dbab24a4650"} {"question" "q-325927" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053984/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c35c5c96549a22aec3fa395d4dac4dd4019a49651a81abae6a45792d1ad3398a"} {"question" "q-325927" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053984/state.json" "file_sha256" "5292b9c37a5f7aeb99349d58f34defbe238b8d16bcf2408d3f4f1dbab24a4650"} {"question" "q-325927" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\sqrt{6}\\sec(t)"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053984/state.json" "file_sha256" "5292b9c37a5f7aeb99349d58f34defbe238b8d16bcf2408d3f4f1dbab24a4650"} {"question" "q-325927" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053984/state.json" "file_sha256" "5292b9c37a5f7aeb99349d58f34defbe238b8d16bcf2408d3f4f1dbab24a4650"} {"question" "q-325927" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053984/state.json" "file_sha256" "5292b9c37a5f7aeb99349d58f34defbe238b8d16bcf2408d3f4f1dbab24a4650"} {"question" "q-106528" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the Cartesian equation of the hyperbola $x=5\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,y=2\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{tan}⁡t.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053984/state.json" "file_sha256" "5292b9c37a5f7aeb99349d58f34defbe238b8d16bcf2408d3f4f1dbab24a4650"} {"question" "q-106528" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the Cartesian equation of the hyperbola, we need to eliminate the parameter $t.$ We can do this using the secant-tangent identity.\n\n- Isolating the $\\operatorname{sec}⁡t$ term in the $x$-equation and squaring, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =5\\operatorname{sec}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{x}{5} & =\\operatorname{sec}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{(5)^{2}} & ={sec}^{2}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{25} & ={sec}^{2}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Isolating the $\\operatorname{tan}⁡t$ term in the $y$-equation and squaring, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =2\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{tan}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{y}{2\\sqrt{3}} & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{(2\\sqrt{3})^{2}} & ={tan}^{2}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{12} & ={tan}^{2}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the two equations into the identity ${tan}^{2}⁡t+1={sec}^{2}⁡t$ and rearranging, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{tan}^{2}⁡t+1 & ={sec}^{2}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{12}+1 & =\\frac{{x}^{2}}{25} \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{25}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{12} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053984/state.json" "file_sha256" "5292b9c37a5f7aeb99349d58f34defbe238b8d16bcf2408d3f4f1dbab24a4650"} {"question" "q-106528" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053984/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c35c5c96549a22aec3fa395d4dac4dd4019a49651a81abae6a45792d1ad3398a"} {"question" "q-106528" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053984/state.json" "file_sha256" "5292b9c37a5f7aeb99349d58f34defbe238b8d16bcf2408d3f4f1dbab24a4650"} {"question" "q-106528" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{12}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{25}=1"] ["math" "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{25}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{12}=1"] ["math" "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{25}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2\\sqrt{3}}=1"] ["math" "\\frac{{y}^{2}}{12}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{25}=1"] ["math" "\\frac{{y}^{2}}{25}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{12}=1"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053984/state.json" "file_sha256" "5292b9c37a5f7aeb99349d58f34defbe238b8d16bcf2408d3f4f1dbab24a4650"} {"question" "q-106528" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{25}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{12}=1"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053984/state.json" "file_sha256" "5292b9c37a5f7aeb99349d58f34defbe238b8d16bcf2408d3f4f1dbab24a4650"} {"question" "q-89293" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the Cartesian equation of the hyperbola $x=5\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,y=2\\operatorname{tan}⁡t.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053984/state.json" "file_sha256" "5292b9c37a5f7aeb99349d58f34defbe238b8d16bcf2408d3f4f1dbab24a4650"} {"question" "q-89293" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the Cartesian equation of the hyperbola, we need to eliminate the parameter $t.$ We can do this using the secant-tangent identity.\n\n- Isolating the $\\operatorname{sec}⁡t$ term in the $x$-equation and squaring, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =5\\operatorname{sec}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{x}{5} & =\\operatorname{sec}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{{5}^{2}} & ={sec}^{2}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{25} & ={sec}^{2}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Isolating the $\\operatorname{tan}⁡t$ term in the $y$-equation and squaring, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =2\\operatorname{tan}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{y}{2} & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{{2}^{2}} & ={tan}^{2}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{4} & ={tan}^{2}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the two equations into the identity ${tan}^{2}⁡t+1={sec}^{2}⁡t$ and rearranging, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{tan}^{2}⁡t+1 & ={sec}^{2}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}+1 & =\\frac{{x}^{2}}{25} \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{25}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053984/state.json" "file_sha256" "5292b9c37a5f7aeb99349d58f34defbe238b8d16bcf2408d3f4f1dbab24a4650"} {"question" "q-89293" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053984/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c35c5c96549a22aec3fa395d4dac4dd4019a49651a81abae6a45792d1ad3398a"} {"question" "q-89293" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053984/state.json" "file_sha256" "5292b9c37a5f7aeb99349d58f34defbe238b8d16bcf2408d3f4f1dbab24a4650"} {"question" "q-89293" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{25}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}=1"] ["math" "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{25}=1"] ["math" "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{5}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}=1"] ["math" "\\frac{{y}^{2}}{25}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}=1"] ["math" "\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{25}=1"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053984/state.json" "file_sha256" "5292b9c37a5f7aeb99349d58f34defbe238b8d16bcf2408d3f4f1dbab24a4650"} {"question" "q-89293" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{25}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}=1"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053984/state.json" "file_sha256" "5292b9c37a5f7aeb99349d58f34defbe238b8d16bcf2408d3f4f1dbab24a4650"} {"question" "q-325936" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the Cartesian equation of the hyperbola $x=5\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,y=\\sqrt{8}\\operatorname{tan}⁡t.$\n\n{{field-1}}\n$=1$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053984/state.json" "file_sha256" "5292b9c37a5f7aeb99349d58f34defbe238b8d16bcf2408d3f4f1dbab24a4650"} {"question" "q-325936" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the Cartesian equation of the hyperbola, we need to eliminate the parameter $t.$ We can do this using the secant-tangent identity.\n\n- Isolating the $\\operatorname{sec}⁡t$ term in the $x$-equation and squaring, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =5\\operatorname{sec}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{x}{5} & =\\operatorname{sec}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{{5}^{2}} & ={sec}^{2}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{25} & ={sec}^{2}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Isolating the $\\operatorname{tan}⁡t$ term in the $y$-equation and squaring, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\sqrt{8}\\operatorname{tan}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{y}{\\sqrt{8}} & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{(\\sqrt{8})^{2}} & ={tan}^{2}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{8} & ={tan}^{2}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the two equations into the identity ${tan}^{2}⁡t+1={sec}^{2}⁡t$ and rearranging, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{tan}^{2}⁡t+1 & ={sec}^{2}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{8}+1 & =\\frac{{x}^{2}}{25} \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{25}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{8} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053984/state.json" "file_sha256" "5292b9c37a5f7aeb99349d58f34defbe238b8d16bcf2408d3f4f1dbab24a4650"} {"question" "q-325936" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053984/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c35c5c96549a22aec3fa395d4dac4dd4019a49651a81abae6a45792d1ad3398a"} {"question" "q-325936" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053984/state.json" "file_sha256" "5292b9c37a5f7aeb99349d58f34defbe238b8d16bcf2408d3f4f1dbab24a4650"} {"question" "q-325936" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{x^2}{25}-\\frac{y^2}{8}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053984/state.json" "file_sha256" "5292b9c37a5f7aeb99349d58f34defbe238b8d16bcf2408d3f4f1dbab24a4650"} {"question" "q-106522" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the Cartesian equation of the hyperbola $x=\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,y=4\\operatorname{tan}⁡t.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053984/state.json" "file_sha256" "5292b9c37a5f7aeb99349d58f34defbe238b8d16bcf2408d3f4f1dbab24a4650"} {"question" "q-106522" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the Cartesian equation of the hyperbola, we need to eliminate the parameter $t.$ We can do this using the secant-tangent identity.\n\n- Isolating the $\\operatorname{sec}⁡t$ term in the $x$-equation and squaring, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sec}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{x}{\\sqrt{3}} & =\\operatorname{sec}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{(\\sqrt{3})^{2}} & ={sec}^{2}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{3} & ={sec}^{2}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Isolating the $\\operatorname{tan}⁡t$ term in the $y$-equation and squaring, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =4\\operatorname{tan}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{y}{4} & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{{4}^{2}} & ={tan}^{2}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{16} & ={tan}^{2}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the two equations into the identity ${tan}^{2}⁡t+1={sec}^{2}⁡t$ and rearranging, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{tan}^{2}⁡t+1 & ={sec}^{2}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{16}+1 & =\\frac{{x}^{2}}{3} \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{3}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{16} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053984/state.json" "file_sha256" "5292b9c37a5f7aeb99349d58f34defbe238b8d16bcf2408d3f4f1dbab24a4650"} {"question" "q-106522" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053984/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c35c5c96549a22aec3fa395d4dac4dd4019a49651a81abae6a45792d1ad3398a"} {"question" "q-106522" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053984/state.json" "file_sha256" "5292b9c37a5f7aeb99349d58f34defbe238b8d16bcf2408d3f4f1dbab24a4650"} {"question" "q-106522" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{16}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{3}=1"] ["math" "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{3}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{16}=1"] ["math" "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{\\sqrt{3}}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}=1"] ["math" "\\frac{{y}^{2}}{3}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{16}=1"] ["math" "\\frac{{y}^{2}}{\\sqrt{3}}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}=1"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053984/state.json" "file_sha256" "5292b9c37a5f7aeb99349d58f34defbe238b8d16bcf2408d3f4f1dbab24a4650"} {"question" "q-106522" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{3}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{16}=1"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053984/state.json" "file_sha256" "5292b9c37a5f7aeb99349d58f34defbe238b8d16bcf2408d3f4f1dbab24a4650"} {"question" "q-106527" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the Cartesian equation of the hyperbola $x=3\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,y=\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{tan}⁡t.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053984/state.json" "file_sha256" "5292b9c37a5f7aeb99349d58f34defbe238b8d16bcf2408d3f4f1dbab24a4650"} {"question" "q-106527" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the Cartesian equation of the hyperbola, we need to eliminate the parameter $t.$ We can do this using the secant-tangent identity.\n\n- Isolating the $\\operatorname{sec}⁡t$ term in the $x$-equation and squaring, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =3\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sec}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{x}{3\\sqrt{2}} & =\\operatorname{sec}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{(3\\sqrt{2})^{2}} & ={sec}^{2}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{18} & ={sec}^{2}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Isolating the $\\operatorname{tan}⁡t$ term in the $y$-equation and squaring, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{tan}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{y}{\\sqrt{3}} & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{(\\sqrt{3})^{2}} & ={tan}^{2}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{3} & ={tan}^{2}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the two equations into the identity ${tan}^{2}⁡t+1={sec}^{2}⁡t$ and rearranging, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{tan}^{2}⁡t+1 & ={sec}^{2}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{3}+1 & =\\frac{{x}^{2}}{18} \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{18}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{3} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053984/state.json" "file_sha256" "5292b9c37a5f7aeb99349d58f34defbe238b8d16bcf2408d3f4f1dbab24a4650"} {"question" "q-106527" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053984/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c35c5c96549a22aec3fa395d4dac4dd4019a49651a81abae6a45792d1ad3398a"} {"question" "q-106527" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053984/state.json" "file_sha256" "5292b9c37a5f7aeb99349d58f34defbe238b8d16bcf2408d3f4f1dbab24a4650"} {"question" "q-106527" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{18}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{3}=1"] ["math" "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{36}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}=1"] ["math" "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{3}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{18}=1"] ["math" "\\frac{{y}^{2}}{18}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{3}=1"] ["math" "\\frac{{y}^{2}}{3}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{18}=1"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053984/state.json" "file_sha256" "5292b9c37a5f7aeb99349d58f34defbe238b8d16bcf2408d3f4f1dbab24a4650"} {"question" "q-106527" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{18}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{3}=1"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053984/state.json" "file_sha256" "5292b9c37a5f7aeb99349d58f34defbe238b8d16bcf2408d3f4f1dbab24a4650"} {"question" "q-325980" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053984/assets/7db943c53e70d9b77490c2d73acac939be08fdfa4b0aa958addb2d50b6078543.png)\n\nOne branch of a hyperbola (shown above) is defined by the parametric equations\n\n$$\nx=3\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,y=\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{tan}⁡t.\n$$\n\nWhat is the domain of the parameter $t?$\n\n$t\\in [$\n$-\\pi ,$\n{{field-1}}$)⋃($\n{{field-2}}\n$,$\n{{field-3}}$]$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053984/state.json" "file_sha256" "5292b9c37a5f7aeb99349d58f34defbe238b8d16bcf2408d3f4f1dbab24a4650"} {"question" "q-325980" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The parametric equations of the full hyperbola are\n\n$$\nx=3\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,y=\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,t\\in [-\\pi ,\\pi ],\\,t\\ne \\pm \\frac{\\pi }{2}.\n$$\n\nTo restrict the parameterization to a single branch, we refer to the diagram below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053984/assets/e03130cdcae3fff94036453883eb638371b62a4ee26b9b550192aed32f95a39d.png)\n\nWe can see that if we restrict $t$ to $[-\\pi ,-\\frac{\\pi }{2})$ and $(\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\pi ],$ we get only the left branch.\n\nTherefore, the parametric equations that describe only the left branch are\n\n$$\nx=3\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,y=\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,t\\in [-\\pi ,-\\frac{\\pi }{2})\\text{ }\\cup \\text{ }(\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\pi ].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053984/state.json" "file_sha256" "5292b9c37a5f7aeb99349d58f34defbe238b8d16bcf2408d3f4f1dbab24a4650"} {"question" "q-325980" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053984/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c35c5c96549a22aec3fa395d4dac4dd4019a49651a81abae6a45792d1ad3398a"} {"question" "q-325980" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053984/state.json" "file_sha256" "5292b9c37a5f7aeb99349d58f34defbe238b8d16bcf2408d3f4f1dbab24a4650"} {"question" "q-325980" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{\\pi}{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053984/state.json" "file_sha256" "5292b9c37a5f7aeb99349d58f34defbe238b8d16bcf2408d3f4f1dbab24a4650"} {"question" "q-325980" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053984/state.json" "file_sha256" "5292b9c37a5f7aeb99349d58f34defbe238b8d16bcf2408d3f4f1dbab24a4650"} {"question" "q-325980" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\pi}{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053984/state.json" "file_sha256" "5292b9c37a5f7aeb99349d58f34defbe238b8d16bcf2408d3f4f1dbab24a4650"} {"question" "q-325980" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" 